❓ Q15. What is the difference between /etc/hosts and /etc/resolv.conf?
File	Purpose
/etc/hosts	Local static hostname-to-IP mapping (checked first)
/etc/resolv.conf	Defines DNS nameservers for external resolution
✅ Pro Answer: "When resolving a hostname, Linux checks /etc/hosts first, then queries DNS servers defined in /etc/resolv.conf. The order is controlled by /etc/nsswitch.conf."

