❓ Q17. What is sudo and how does it work?
✅ Model Answer:

"sudo (Superuser Do) allows a permitted user to run commands as root or another user without knowing the root password. Permissions are configured in /etc/sudoers (edited via visudo). It logs all commands for auditing, making it safer than logging in as root."

