📊 SECTION 6: Performance Troubleshooting (Mid/Senior Level)
❓ Q19. Server is slow — what steps do you take?
✅ This is a top interview question — here's the perfect structured answer:

"I follow a systematic top-down approach:"

Copy# Step 1: Check overall load
uptime              # Load average (1, 5, 15 min)
top / htop          # Real-time CPU & memory

# Step 2: Check CPU
vmstat 1 5          # CPU, memory, I/O stats every 1 sec
mpstat -P ALL       # Per-core CPU usage

# Step 3: Check Memory
free -h             # RAM & swap usage
cat /proc/meminfo   # Detailed memory stats

# Step 4: Check Disk I/O
iostat -xz 1        # Disk I/O statistics
iotop               # Top disk-using processes

# Step 5: Check Network
netstat -s          # Network statistics
iftop               # Network bandwidth usage

# Step 6: Check Logs
dmesg | tail -50          # Kernel messages
tail -f /var/log/syslog   # System logs
journalctl -xe            # Systemd logs
💡 The interviewer wants to see your structured thinking, not just one command.

