🔧 SECTION 7: Advanced Topics (Senior/DevOps Level)
❓ Q21. What is LVM (Logical Volume Manager)?
✅ Model Answer:

"LVM provides a flexible disk management layer that allows you to resize, snapshot, and manage storage without downtime. It abstracts physical disks into logical volumes."

Layers: Physical Volume (PV) → Volume Group (VG) → Logical Volume (LV)

Copypvcreate /dev/sdb         # Create physical volume
vgcreate vg_data /dev/sdb # Create volume group
lvcreate -L 50G -n lv_app vg_data  # Create logical volume
lvextend -L +20G /dev/vg_data/lv_app  # Resize
resize2fs /dev/vg_data/lv_app         # Extend filesystem
